ritmias, isquemia/necrose, extravasamento, hipertensão grave y redução de perfusão de órgãos.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"contraindications\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Hipersensibilidade y contraindicações específicas da bula.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"interactions\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Revisar interações farmacodinâmicas y metabólicas aplicáveis.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"monitoring\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Monitorar eficácia, tolerabilidade, función orgânica y eventos graves.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"administration\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Usar somente via/formulação rotulada; respeitar técnica y alimentos.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"preparation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Confirmar concentração, diluição y estabilidade no produto; no inferir.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"infusionProtocol\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Quando IV, usar bomba/monitorização y protocolo da bula; caso contrário no aplicável.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pregnancy\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Avaliar riesgo fetal, indicação y bula.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"lactation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Avaliar excreção y riesgo-benefício.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"specialPopulations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Individualizar em idosos, comorbidades, gestação y disfunción orgânica.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"patientEducation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Orientar adesão, sinais de alarme y no interromper abruptamente quando aplicável.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"clinicalPearls\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Formulações y combinações no são automaticamente intercambiáveis.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"guidelineRecommendations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Usar conforme diretriz oficial da indicação y jurisdição.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"safetyFlags\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Arritmias, isquemia/necrose, extravasamento, hipertensão grave y redução de perfusão de órgãos.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"alerts\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Arritmias, isquemia/necrose, extravasamento, hipertensão grave y redução de perfusão de órgãos.; monitorização obrigatória\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"references\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Fonte primária/oficial - https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?query=norepinephrine\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Fonte primária/oficial - https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2020/007513s038lbl.pdf\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"ref\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?query=norepinephrine\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"pt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Noradrenalina\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"es\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Noradrenalina\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"keywords\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"noradrenalina\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"noradrenalina (hemitartarato de)\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"dataVersion\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"clinical-data-v1-b2437901deb78b1e\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"clinicalContentSha256\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"b2437901deb78b1eeb3119ee415221916ce300d3c825122141897d5b793b513d\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"medcases-calculadora\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"schema\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"legacy-v1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sourceModule\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"emergencia.js\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"mc_clinical_enrichment_v1\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"schema\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"medcases.clinical-enrichment.v1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"drug_key\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"noradrenalina\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"stage_a_batch\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"04\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"stage_a_reviewed_at\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-08-24\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"stage_a_source_policy\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"official_regulatory_label_admin_preparation_references\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sections\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"administracao_preparo\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"pt\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Diluição\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Diluir antes da administração. A rotulagem consultada orienta preparo em dextrose 5% ou em solução de cloreto de sódio que contenha 5% de dextrose; solução salina isolada não é recomendada para essa apresentação concentrada.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Acesso venoso\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infundir em veia calibrosa e verificar frequentemente o local de infusão para reduzir o risco de extravasamento e necrose tecidual.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Estabilidade / compatibilidade\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"A solução diluída pode ser mantida por até 24 horas em temperatura ambiente, protegida da luz. Evitar contato com sais de ferro, álcalis ou agentes oxidantes.\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"es\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Dilución\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Diluir antes de administrar. El rotulado consultado indica preparación en dextrosa al 5% o en solución de cloruro de sodio que contenga 5% de dextrosa; la solución salina sola no se recomienda para esta presentación concentrada.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Acceso venoso\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infundir en una vena de buen calibre y comprobar frecuentemente el sitio de infusión para reducir el riesgo de extravasación y necrosis tisular.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Estabilidad / compatibilidad\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"La solución diluida puede mantenerse hasta 24 horas a temperatura ambiente, protegida de la luz. Evitar contacto con sales de hierro, álcalis o agentes oxidantes.\\\\\\\"}]},\\\\\\\"referencias\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"pt\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DailyMed — Norepinephrine Bitartrate Injection\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Fonte oficial/regulatória consultada em 24/08/2026 para Administração/Preparo.\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"es\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DailyMed — Norepinephrine Bitartrate Injection\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Fuente oficial/regulatoria consultada el 24/08/2026 para Administración/Preparación.\\\\\\\"}]}},\\\\\\\"sources\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"stage\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"A_BATCH04\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"dailymed_norepinephrine_4408987e\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DailyMed — Norepinephrine Bitartrate Injection\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=4408987e-690a-41ac-9677-e24604fa9793\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"reviewed_at\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-08-24\\\\\\\"}]},\\\\\\\"mc_gold_standard_v1\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PASS_CLINICAL_HOMOLOGATION\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sourceOwner\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"database/emergencia.js\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sourceField\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"noradrenalina.mcGoldClinicalV1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"lote\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"056\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"requiredFields\\\\\\\":33,\\\\\\\"approvedSha256\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"498cafa4e0fbd5a28b86b77472df89a94eaa0fa96bde0eb3b706fdf18d0e7236\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"calculationAuthorized\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\"publicationAuthorized\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"clinicalPackagePublicationState\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"BLOQUEADA\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ownerPublicationAuthorization\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"lote002-owner-confirmed\\\\\\\"}}\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"# Noradrenalina\\\\n\\\\n## Clase\\\\n\\\\nVasopressor agonista alfa-adrenérgico predominante\\\\n\\\\n## Clase farmacológica\\\\n\\\\nVasopressor agonista alfa-adrenérgico predominante\\\\n\\\\n## Nombres comerciales\\\\n\\\\nMarcas variam por país.\\\\n\\\\n## Presentación\\\\n\\\\nConcentrados y bolsas prontas em concentrações diversas; no inferir equivalência.\\\\n\\\\n## Presentaciones\\\\n\\\\nConcentrados y bolsas prontas em concentrações diversas; no inferir equivalência.\\\\n\\\\n## Mecanismo\\\\n\\\\nMecanismo específico da classe conforme fonte primária y formulação.\\\\n\\\\n## Farmacodinámica\\\\n\\\\nMecanismo específico da classe conforme fonte primária y formulação.\\\\n\\\\n## Farmacocinética\\\\n\\\\nRevisar absorção, metabolismo, meia-vida y eliminação na fonte primária.\\\\n\\\\n## Indicaciones\\\\n\\\\nRestauração da pressão arterial em hipotensão aguda grave após correção adequada da hipovolemia.\\\\n\\\\n## Posología de referencia\\\\n\\\\nInfusão IV titulada à meta hemodinâmica. Rótulos históricos iniciam 8-12 microgramas/min y mantêm 2-4 microgramas/min, mas protocolos por peso y concentrações variam; exigir concentração, acesso, bomba y monitorização explícitos.\\\\n\\\\n## Pediatría\\\\n\\\\nRequer tabela completa por idade/peso; automação pediátrica bloqueada.\\\\n\\\\n## Función renal\\\\n\\\\nAvaliar función renal y tabela específica; no inferir ajuste.\\\\n\\\\n## Función hepática\\\\n\\\\nAvaliar hepatopatia; no inferir ajuste.\\\\n\\\\n## Efectos adversos comunes\\\\n\\\\nIsquemia periférica, ansiedade, cefaleia, dispneia y bradicardia reflexa.\\\\n\\\\n## Efectos adversos graves\\\\n\\\\nArritmias, isquemia/necrose, extravasamento, hipertensão grave y redução de perfusão de órgãos.\\\\n\\\\n## Efectos adversos\\\\n\\\\nIsquemia periférica, ansiedade, cefaleia, dispneia y bradicardia reflexa.; Arritmias, isquemia/necrose, extravasamento, hipertensão grave y redução de perfusão de órgãos.\\\\n\\\\n## Contraindicaciones\\\\n\\\\nHipersensibilidade y contraindicações específicas da bula.\\\\n\\\\n## Interacciones\\\\n\\\\nRevisar interações farmacodinâmicas y metabólicas aplicáveis.\\\\n\\\\n## Monitorización\\\\n\\\\nMonitorar eficácia, tolerabilidade, función orgânica y eventos graves.\\\\n\\\\n## Administración\\\\n\\\\nUsar somente via/formulação rotulada; respeitar técnica y alimentos.\\\\n\\\\n## Preparación\\\\n\\\\nConfirmar concentração, diluição y estabilidade no produto; no inferir.\\\\n\\\\n## Infusión\\\\n\\\\nQuando IV, usar bomba/monitorização y protocolo da bula; caso contrário no aplicável.\\\\n\\\\n## Embarazo\\\\n\\\\nAvaliar riesgo fetal, indicação y bula.\\\\n\\\\n## Lactancia\\\\n\\\\nAvaliar excreção y riesgo-benefício.\\\\n\\\\n## Poblaciones especiales\\\\n\\\\nIndividualizar em idosos, comorbidades, gestação y disfunción orgânica.\\\\n\\\\n## Orientación\\\\n\\\\nOrientar adesão, sinais de alarme y no interromper abruptamente quando aplicável.\\\\n\\\\n## Observaciones clínicas\\\\n\\\\nFormulações y combinações no são automaticamente intercambiáveis.\\\\n\\\\n## Guías\\\\n\\\\nUsar conforme diretriz oficial da indicação y jurisdição.\\\\n\\\\n## Seguridad\\\\n\\\\nArritmias, isquemia/necrose, extravasamento, hipertensão grave y redução de perfusão de órgãos.\\\\n\\\\n## Alertas\\\\n\\\\nArritmias, isquemia/necrose, extravasamento, hipertensão grave y redução de perfusão de órgãos.; monitorização obrigatória\\\\n\\\\n## Referencias\\\\n\\\\nFonte primária/oficial - https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?query=norepinephrine\\\\n\\\\nFonte primária/oficial - https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2020/007513s038lbl.pdf\\\\n\\\\n## Referencia\\\\n\\\\nhttps://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?query=norepinephrine\\\",\\\"calculationAuthorized\\\":false,\\\"clinicalApprovalGranted\\\":false}\",\"payloadSha256\":\"347e953a5bb3eac3ee955fa7008232581f519935622b27036a83b9ba23015a33\",\"modelCalls\":0},\"ceftriaxona/pt\":{\"documentJson\":\"{\\\"scope\\\":\\\"CANONICAL_DRUG_INFORMATION_NOT_PRESCRIPTION\\\",\\\"language\\\":\\\"pt\\\",\\\"canonicalDrugId\\\":\\\"ceftriaxona\\\",\\\"sourceVersion\\\":\\\"clinical-data-v1-b2437901deb78b1e\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"medcases-calculadora\\\",\\\"sourceContentHash\\\":\\\"b2437901deb78b1eeb3119ee415221916ce300d3c825122141897d5b793b513d\\\",\\\"sourceJson\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"infectologia\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"icon\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"color\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"colorTxt\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"pt\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"class\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cefalosporina de 3ª geração parenteral\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pharmacologicClass\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Beta-lactâmico inibidor da síntese da parede bacteriana\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"mechanism\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Beta-lactâmico inibidor da síntese da parede bacteriana. O efeito deve ser interpretado por indicação, formulação e exposição.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pharmacodynamics\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Resposta e toxicidade dependem da exposição e população; consultar dose e monitorização.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pharmacokinetics\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Meia-vida longa; eliminação renal e biliar; alta ligação proteica.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"indications\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infecções suscetíveis sistêmicas, meningite, gonorreia e profilaxia cirúrgica conforme protocolo.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"commercialNames\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Não presumir marca regional; usar somente produto correspondente às fontes regulatórias citadas.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"presentation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Frascos 250/500 mg, 1 g e 2 g para IV/IM.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"presentations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Frascos 250/500 mg, 1 g e 2 g para IV/IM.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"dose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Adulto: 1-2 g IV/IM uma vez/dia ou dividido; grave/meningite até 4 g/dia. Gonorreia: seguir guideline vigente.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pediatricDose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"50-75 mg/kg/dia; meningite 100 mg/kg/dia, máximo 4 g/dia. Neonatos têm restrições específicas. AUTOMATABLE=NO.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"renalDose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Geralmente sem ajuste renal isolado; limitar/monitorar se disfunção renal e hepática combinadas.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"hepaticDose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cautela em doença grave e disfunção renal concomitante.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"commonAdverseEffects\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Diarreia, náusea, rash e reação no local de administração.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"dangerousAdverseEffects\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsões por acúmulo e lesão orgânica rara.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"adverseEffects\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Diarreia, náusea, rash e reação no local de administração. Graves: Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsões por acúmulo e lesão orgânica rara.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"contraindications\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Hipersensibilidade grave a cefalosporinas; avaliar reação imediata a outros beta-lactâmicos.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"interactions\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Probenecida pode elevar exposição; revisar anticoagulantes, nefrotóxicos, soluções incompatíveis e vacinas bacterianas vivas.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"monitoring\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Culturas e suscetibilidade, resposta, alergia, C. difficile, hemograma, função renal/hepática e neurotoxicidade.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"administration\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"IV/IM; nunca misturar ou coadministrar com cálcio IV em neonatos.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"preparation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Reconstituir conforme via; lidocaína apenas IM e nunca IV.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"infusionProtocol\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"IV em cerca de 30 min; usar linha separada/lavada para soluções com cálcio fora do período neonatal.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pregnancy\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Usar quando indicado após avaliação de benefício-risco.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"lactation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Passagem geralmente baixa; observar diarreia, candidíase ou sensibilização no lactente.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"specialPopulations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ver pediatria, função renal/hepática, gestação, lactação e idosos; individualizar fragilidade e polifarmácia.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"patientEducation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Explicar indicação, administração, adesão e sinais de alarme; não alterar dose sem orientação.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"clinicalPearls\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Confirmar produto, concentração, via, indicação, peso e função orgânica antes de calcular ou administrar.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"guidelineRecommendations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Conteúdo ancorado em bula regulatória primária; protocolo local e microbiologia podem restringir uso.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"safetyFlags\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"CANDIDATO NÃO HOMOLOGADO. Revisão médica obrigatória antes de integração.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"alerts\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsões por acúmulo e lesão orgânica rara. Uso bloqueado em neonatos sem idade/bilirrubina/cálcio IV; demais doses bloqueadas sem foco, peso, alergia e função renal/hepática.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"references\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"1. Fonte regulatória primária consultada em 2026-09-18: https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?labeltype=human&query=ceftriaxone\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"2. Fonte regulatória primária consultada em 2026-09-18: https://www.cdc.gov/std/treatment-guidelines/gonorrhea-adults.htm\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"ref\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?labeltype=human&query=ceftriaxone\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"es\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"class\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cefalosporina de 3ª generación parenteral\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pharmacologicClass\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Betalactámico inhibidor de la síntesis de pared bacteriana\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"mechanism\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Betalactámico inhibidor de la síntesis de pared bacteriana. El efecto debe interpretarse por indicación, formulación y exposición.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pharmacodynamics\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Respuesta y toxicidad dependen de exposición y población; consultar dosis y monitorización.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pharmacokinetics\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Semivida larga; eliminación renal y biliar; alta unión proteica.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"indications\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infecciones sistémicas susceptibles, meningitis, gonorrea y profilaxis quirúrgica según protocolo.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"commercialNames\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"No presumir marca regional; usar solo producto correspondiente a fuentes regulatorias citadas.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"presentation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Viales 250/500 mg, 1 g y 2 g para IV/IM.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"presentations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Viales 250/500 mg, 1 g y 2 g para IV/IM.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"dose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Adulto: 1-2 g IV/IM una vez/día o dividido; grave/meningitis hasta 4 g/día. Gonorrea: seguir guía vigente.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pediatricDose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"50-75 mg/kg/día; meningitis 100 mg/kg/día, máximo 4 g/día. Neonatos tienen restricciones específicas. AUTOMATABLE=NO.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"renalDose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Generalmente sin ajuste renal aislado; limitar/controlar si disfunción renal y hepática combinadas.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"hepaticDose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Precaución en enfermedad grave y disfunción renal concomitante.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"commonAdverseEffects\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Diarrea, náusea, erupción y reacción en sitio de administración.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"dangerousAdverseEffects\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsiones por acumulación y lesión orgánica rara.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"adverseEffects\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Diarrea, náusea, erupción y reacción en sitio de administración. Graves: Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsiones por acumulación y lesión orgánica rara.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"contraindications\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Hipersensibilidad grave a cefalosporinas; evaluar reacción inmediata a otros betalactámicos.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"interactions\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Probenecid puede elevar exposición; revisar anticoagulantes, nefrotóxicos, soluciones incompatibles y vacunas bacterianas vivas.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"monitoring\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cultivos y sensibilidad, respuesta, alergia, C. difficile, hemograma, función renal/hepática y neurotoxicidad.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"administration\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"IV/IM; nunca mezclar o coadministrar con calcio IV en neonatos.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"preparation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Reconstituir según vía; lidocaína solo IM y nunca IV.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"infusionProtocol\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"IV en unos 30 min; usar línea separada/lavada para soluciones con calcio fuera del período neonatal.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pregnancy\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Usar cuando esté indicado tras evaluar beneficio-riesgo.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"lactation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Paso generalmente bajo; vigilar diarrea, candidiasis o sensibilización en lactante.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"specialPopulations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ver pediatría, función renal/hepática, embarazo, lactancia y ancianos; individualizar fragilidad y polifarmacia.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"patientEducation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Explicar indicación, administración, adherencia y signos de alarma; no cambiar dosis sin indicación.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"clinicalPearls\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Confirmar producto, concentración, vía, indicación, peso y función orgánica antes de calcular o administrar.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"guidelineRecommendations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Contenido basado en ficha regulatoria primaria; protocolo local y microbiología pueden restringir uso.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"safetyFlags\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"CANDIDATO NO HOMOLOGADO. Revisión médica obligatoria antes de integración.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"alerts\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsiones por acumulación y lesión orgánica rara. Uso bloqueado em neonatos sem idade/bilirrubina/cálcio IV; demais doses bloqueadas sem foco, peso, alergia e função renal/hepática.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"references\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"1. Fonte regulatória primária consultada em 2026-09-18: https://dailymed.nlm