nsiderar límite de dosis (≤2 g/día) y monitorización intensificada.\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"hemodialise\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"vo\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"ev\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"dose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"1–2 g\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"intervalo\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"24/24h\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"doseMaxima\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"4 g/dia\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"unidade\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"g\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"pediatrica\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"dose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"50–100 mg/kg\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"intervalo\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"24/24h\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"doseMaxima\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"4 g/dia\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"unidade\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"mg/kg\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"obs\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"No requiere dosis suplementaria post-hemodiálisis. Altamente ligada a proteínas — no dializable.\\\\\\\"}},\\\\\\\"safetyFlags\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"renalHighRisk\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\"neurotoxicityRisk\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\"qtRisk\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\"hepatotoxicityRisk\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"requiresCultureGuidance\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\"warning\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Evitar en neonatos con hiperbilirrubinemia o uso concomitante de calcio EV (riesgo de precipitación fatal). En insuficiencia hepática y renal combinadas graves, limitar dosis a ≤2 g/día.\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"auditNotes\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"excellent_after_review\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sourcePriority\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"FDA label Rocephin (ceftriaxone) 2022\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"EMA label Ceftriaxona 2022\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Sanford Guide to Antimicrobial Therapy 2025\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Johns Hopkins ABX Guide 2024\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"UpToDate 2024\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Lexicomp Online 2025\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Goodman & Gilman's Pharmacological Basis of Therapeutics 14ª ed.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"note\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Bloque fusionado y mejorado: message corregida a 'aislado'; fgMaior50.obs con meningitis 12/12h; fgMenor10.obs con límite de dosis ≤2 g/día en IR+IH combinadas; hemodialise.obs con 'no dializable'; safetyFlags y auditNotes añadidos.\\\\\\\"}},\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"pt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"es\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ceftriaxona\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"keywords\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"rocefin\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona eurofarma\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona abl\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"rocephin\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona richet\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona generica\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"cefalosporina de 3ª geracao\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"dataVersion\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"clinical-data-v1-e61729424f211913\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"clinicalContentSha256\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"e61729424f2119133df2859fd54b61485ca0d422f660b50949e686e5f2e0905e\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"medcases-calculadora\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"schema\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"premium-v1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sourceModule\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"antimicrobianos.js\\\\\\\"}}],\\\\\\\"mc_clinical_enrichment_v1\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"schema\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"medcases.clinical-enrichment.v1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"drug_key\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"stage_a_batch\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"05\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"stage_a_reviewed_at\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-08-24\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"stage_a_source_policy\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"official_regulatory_label_admin_preparation_references\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sections\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"administracao_preparo\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"pt\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infusão IV\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Administrar por infusão intravenosa ao longo de 30 minutos; em neonatos, utilizar 60 minutos conforme a rotulagem da apresentação.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cálcio — incompatibilidade\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Não reconstituir nem diluir com soluções contendo cálcio, como Ringer ou Hartmann. Não administrar simultaneamente com soluções IV contendo cálcio na mesma linha; em pacientes não neonatais, uso sequencial requer lavagem completa da linha com fluido compatível.\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"es\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infusión IV\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Administrar mediante infusión intravenosa durante 30 minutos; en neonatos, utilizar 60 minutos según el rotulado de la presentación.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Calcio — incompatibilidad\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"No reconstituir ni diluir con soluciones que contengan calcio, como Ringer o Hartmann. No administrar simultáneamente con soluciones IV que contengan calcio por la misma línea; en pacientes no neonatales, el uso secuencial requiere lavado completo de la línea con un fluido compatible.\\\\\\\"}]},\\\\\\\"referencias\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"pt\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DailyMed — Ceftriaxone Sodium for Injection\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Fonte oficial/regulatória consultada em 24/08/2026 para Administração/Preparo. Atualização da fonte informada: 2026-01-22.\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"es\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DailyMed — Ceftriaxone Sodium for Injection\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Fuente oficial/regulatoria consultada el 24/08/2026 para Administración/Preparación. Actualización informada de la fuente: 2026-01-22.\\\\\\\"}]}},\\\\\\\"sources\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"stage\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"A_BATCH05\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"dailymed_ceftriaxone_128bb292\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DailyMed — Ceftriaxone Sodium for Injection\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=128bb292-d174-4769-b3e6-9f16617f31e3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"reviewed_at\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-08-24\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"updated\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-01-22\\\\\\\"}]},\\\\\\\"mc_gold_standard_v1\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PASS_CLINICAL_HOMOLOGATION\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sourceOwner\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"database/infectologia.js\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sourceField\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona.mcGoldClinicalV1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"lote\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"016\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"requiredFields\\\\\\\":33,\\\\\\\"approvedSha256\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"edd955962363f9efc0d22d2a79299d1e785692bced8bf248426d86777ef530d0\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"calculationAuthorized\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\"publicationAuthorized\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"clinicalPackagePublicationState\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"NAO_AUTORIZADA\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ownerPublicationAuthorization\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"mission10-owner-confirmed\\\\\\\"}}\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"# Ceftriaxona\\\\n\\\\n## Classe\\\\n\\\\nCefalosporina de 3ª geração parenteral\\\\n\\\\n## Classe farmacológica\\\\n\\\\nBeta-lactâmico inibidor da síntese da parede bacteriana\\\\n\\\\n## Mecanismo\\\\n\\\\nBeta-lactâmico inibidor da síntese da parede bacteriana. O efeito deve ser interpretado por indicação, formulação e exposição.\\\\n\\\\n## Farmacodinâmica\\\\n\\\\nResposta e toxicidade dependem da exposição e população; consultar dose e monitorização.\\\\n\\\\n## Farmacocinética\\\\n\\\\nMeia-vida longa; eliminação renal e biliar; alta ligação proteica.\\\\n\\\\n## Indicações\\\\n\\\\nInfecções suscetíveis sistêmicas, meningite, gonorreia e profilaxia cirúrgica conforme protocolo.\\\\n\\\\n## Nomes comerciais\\\\n\\\\nNão presumir marca regional; usar somente produto correspondente às fontes regulatórias citadas.\\\\n\\\\n## Apresentação\\\\n\\\\nFrascos 250/500 mg, 1 g e 2 g para IV/IM.\\\\n\\\\n## Apresentações\\\\n\\\\nFrascos 250/500 mg, 1 g e 2 g para IV/IM.\\\\n\\\\n## Posologia de referência\\\\n\\\\nAdulto: 1-2 g IV/IM uma vez/dia ou dividido; grave/meningite até 4 g/dia. Gonorreia: seguir guideline vigente.\\\\n\\\\n## Pediatria\\\\n\\\\n50-75 mg/kg/dia; meningite 100 mg/kg/dia, máximo 4 g/dia. Neonatos têm restrições específicas. AUTOMATABLE=NO.\\\\n\\\\n## Função renal\\\\n\\\\nGeralmente sem ajuste renal isolado; limitar/monitorar se disfunção renal e hepática combinadas.\\\\n\\\\n## Função hepática\\\\n\\\\nCautela em doença grave e disfunção renal concomitante.\\\\n\\\\n## Efeitos adversos comuns\\\\n\\\\nDiarreia, náusea, rash e reação no local de administração.\\\\n\\\\n## Efeitos adversos graves\\\\n\\\\nAnafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsões por acúmulo e lesão orgânica rara.\\\\n\\\\n## Efeitos adversos\\\\n\\\\nDiarreia, náusea, rash e reação no local de administração. Graves: Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsões por acúmulo e lesão orgânica rara.\\\\n\\\\n## Contraindicações\\\\n\\\\nHipersensibilidade grave a cefalosporinas; avaliar reação imediata a outros beta-lactâmicos.\\\\n\\\\n## Interações\\\\n\\\\nProbenecida pode elevar exposição; revisar anticoagulantes, nefrotóxicos, soluções incompatíveis e vacinas bacterianas vivas.\\\\n\\\\n## Monitorização\\\\n\\\\nCulturas e suscetibilidade, resposta, alergia, C. difficile, hemograma, função renal/hepática e neurotoxicidade.\\\\n\\\\n## Administração\\\\n\\\\nIV/IM; nunca misturar ou coadministrar com cálcio IV em neonatos.\\\\n\\\\n## Preparo\\\\n\\\\nReconstituir conforme via; lidocaína apenas IM e nunca IV.\\\\n\\\\n## Infusão\\\\n\\\\nIV em cerca de 30 min; usar linha separada/lavada para soluções com cálcio fora do período neonatal.\\\\n\\\\n## Gestação\\\\n\\\\nUsar quando indicado após avaliação de benefício-risco.\\\\n\\\\n## Lactação\\\\n\\\\nPassagem geralmente baixa; observar diarreia, candidíase ou sensibilização no lactente.\\\\n\\\\n## Populações especiais\\\\n\\\\nVer pediatria, função renal/hepática, gestação, lactação e idosos; individualizar fragilidade e polifarmácia.\\\\n\\\\n## Orientação\\\\n\\\\nExplicar indicação, administração, adesão e sinais de alarme; não alterar dose sem orientação.\\\\n\\\\n## Observações clínicas\\\\n\\\\nConfirmar produto, concentração, via, indicação, peso e função orgânica antes de calcular ou administrar.\\\\n\\\\n## Diretrizes\\\\n\\\\nConteúdo ancorado em bula regulatória primária; protocolo local e microbiologia podem restringir uso.\\\\n\\\\n## Segurança\\\\n\\\\nCANDIDATO NÃO HOMOLOGADO. Revisão médica obrigatória antes de integração.\\\\n\\\\n## Alertas\\\\n\\\\nAnafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsões por acúmulo e lesão orgânica rara. Uso bloqueado em neonatos sem idade/bilirrubina/cálcio IV; demais doses bloqueadas sem foco, peso, alergia e função renal/hepática.\\\\n\\\\n## Referências\\\\n\\\\n1. Fonte regulatória primária consultada em 2026-09-18: https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?labeltype=human&query=ceftriaxone\\\\n\\\\n2. Fonte regulatória primária consultada em 2026-09-18: https://www.cdc.gov/std/treatment-guidelines/gonorrhea-adults.htm\\\\n\\\\n## Referência\\\\n\\\\nhttps://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?labeltype=human&query=ceftriaxone\\\",\\\"calculationAuthorized\\\":false,\\\"clinicalApprovalGranted\\\":false}\",\"payloadSha256\":\"58775cd11ffc9e23468ed4349a9864aec1d9ff8aedb83399becbd350985a6b56\",\"modelCalls\":0},\"ceftriaxona/es\":{\"documentJson\":\"{\\\"scope\\\":\\\"CANONICAL_DRUG_INFORMATION_NOT_PRESCRIPTION\\\",\\\"language\\\":\\\"es\\\",\\\"canonicalDrugId\\\":\\\"ceftriaxona\\\",\\\"sourceVersion\\\":\\\"clinical-data-v1-b2437901deb78b1e\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"medcases-calculadora\\\",\\\"sourceContentHash\\\":\\\"b2437901deb78b1eeb3119ee415221916ce300d3c825122141897d5b793b513d\\\",\\\"sourceJson\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"infectologia\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"icon\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"color\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"colorTxt\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"pt\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"class\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cefalosporina de 3ª geração parenteral\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pharmacologicClass\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Beta-lactâmico inibidor da síntese da parede bacteriana\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"mechanism\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Beta-lactâmico inibidor da síntese da parede bacteriana. O efeito deve ser interpretado por indicação, formulação e exposição.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pharmacodynamics\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Resposta e toxicidade dependem da exposição e população; consultar dose e monitorização.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pharmacokinetics\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Meia-vida longa; eliminação renal e biliar; alta ligação proteica.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"indications\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infecções suscetíveis sistêmicas, meningite, gonorreia e profilaxia cirúrgica conforme protocolo.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"commercialNames\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Não presumir marca regional; usar somente produto correspondente às fontes regulatórias citadas.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"presentation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Frascos 250/500 mg, 1 g e 2 g para IV/IM.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"presentations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Frascos 250/500 mg, 1 g e 2 g para IV/IM.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"dose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Adulto: 1-2 g IV/IM uma vez/dia ou dividido; grave/meningite até 4 g/dia. Gonorreia: seguir guideline vigente.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pediatricDose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"50-75 mg/kg/dia; meningite 100 mg/kg/dia, máximo 4 g/dia. Neonatos têm restrições específicas. AUTOMATABLE=NO.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"renalDose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Geralmente sem ajuste renal isolado; limitar/monitorar se disfunção renal e hepática combinadas.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"hepaticDose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cautela em doença grave e disfunção renal concomitante.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"commonAdverseEffects\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Diarreia, náusea, rash e reação no local de administração.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"dangerousAdverseEffects\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsões por acúmulo e lesão orgânica rara.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"adverseEffects\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Diarreia, náusea, rash e reação no local de administração. Graves: Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsões por acúmulo e lesão orgânica rara.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"contraindications\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Hipersensibilidade grave a cefalosporinas; avaliar reação imediata a outros beta-lactâmicos.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"interactions\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Probenecida pode elevar exposição; revisar anticoagulantes, nefrotóxicos, soluções incompatíveis e vacinas bacterianas vivas.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"monitoring\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Culturas e suscetibilidade, resposta, alergia, C. difficile, hemograma, função renal/hepática e neurotoxicidade.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"administration\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"IV/IM; nunca misturar ou coadministrar com cálcio IV em neonatos.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"preparation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Reconstituir conforme via; lidocaína apenas IM e nunca IV.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"infusionProtocol\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"IV em cerca de 30 min; usar linha separada/lavada para soluções com cálcio fora do período neonatal.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pregnancy\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Usar quando indicado após avaliação de benefício-risco.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"lactation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Passagem geralmente baixa; observar diarreia, candidíase ou sensibilização no lactente.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"specialPopulations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ver pediatria, função renal/hepática, gestação, lactação e idosos; individualizar fragilidade e polifarmácia.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"patientEducation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Explicar indicação, administração, adesão e sinais de alarme; não alterar dose sem orientação.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"clinicalPearls\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Confirmar produto, concentração, via, indicação, peso e função orgânica antes de calcular ou administrar.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"guidelineRecommendations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Conteúdo ancorado em bula regulatória primária; protocolo local e microbiologia podem restringir uso.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"safetyFlags\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"CANDIDATO NÃO HOMOLOGADO. Revisão médica obrigatória antes de integração.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"alerts\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsões por acúmulo e lesão orgânica rara. Uso bloqueado em neonatos sem idade/bilirrubina/cálcio IV; demais doses bloqueadas sem foco, peso, alergia e função renal/hepática.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"references\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"1. Fonte regulatória primária consultada em 2026-09-18: https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?labeltype=human&query=ceftriaxone\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"2. Fonte regulatória primária consultada em 2026-09-18: https://www.cdc.gov/std/treatment-guidelines/gonorrhea-adults.htm\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"ref\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?labeltype=human&query=ceftriaxone\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"es\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"class\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cefalosporina de 3ª generación parenteral\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pharmacologicClass\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Betalactámico inhibidor de la síntesis de pared bacteriana\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"mechanism\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Betalactámico inhibidor de la síntesis de pared bacteriana. El efecto debe interpretarse por indicación, formulación y exposición.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pharmacodynamics\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Respuesta y toxicidad dependen de exposición y población; consultar dosis y monitorización.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pharmacokinetics\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Semivida larga; eliminación renal y biliar; alta unión proteica.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"indications\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infecciones sistémicas susceptibles, meningitis, gonorrea y profilaxis quirúrgica según protocolo.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"commercialNames\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"No presumir marca regional; usar solo producto correspondiente a fuentes regulatorias citadas.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"presentation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Viales 250/500 mg, 1 g y 2 g para IV/IM.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"presentations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Viales 250/500 mg, 1 g y 2 g para IV/IM.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"dose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Adulto: 1-2 g IV/IM una vez/día o dividido; grave/meningitis hasta 4 g/día. Gonorrea: seguir guía vigente.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pediatricDose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"50-75 mg/kg/día; meningitis 100 mg/kg/día, máximo 4 g/día. Neonatos tienen restricciones específicas. AUTOMATABLE=NO.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"renalDose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Generalmente sin ajuste renal aislado; limitar/controlar si disfunción renal y hepática combinadas.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"hepaticDose\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Precaución en enfermedad grave y disfunción renal concomitante.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"commonAdverseEffects\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Diarrea, náusea, erupción y reacción en sitio de administración.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"dangerousAdverseEffects\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsiones por acumulación y lesión orgánica rara.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"adverseEffects\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Diarrea, náusea, erupción y reacción en sitio de administración. Graves: Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsiones por acumulación y lesión orgánica rara.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"contraindications\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Hipersensibilidad grave a cefalosporinas; evaluar reacción inmediata a otros betalactámicos.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"interactions\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Probenecid puede elevar exposición; revisar anticoagulantes, nefrotóxicos, soluciones incompatibles y vacunas bacterianas vivas.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"monitoring\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cultivos y sensibilidad, respuesta, alergia, C. difficile, hemograma, función renal/hepática y neurotoxicidad.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"administration\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"IV/IM; nunca mezclar o coadministrar con calcio IV en neonatos.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"preparation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Reconstituir según vía; lidocaína solo IM y nunca IV.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"infusionProtocol\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"IV en unos 30 min; usar línea separada/lavada para soluciones con calcio fuera del período neonatal.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pregnancy\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Usar cuando esté indicado tras evaluar beneficio-riesgo.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"lactation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Paso generalmente bajo; vigilar diarrea, candidiasis o sensibilización en lactante.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"specialPopulations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ver pediatría, función renal/hepática, embarazo, lactancia y ancianos; individualizar fragilidad y polifarmacia.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"patientEducation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Explicar indicación, administración, adherencia y signos de alarma; no cambiar dosis sin indicación.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"clinicalPearls\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Confirmar producto, concentración, vía, indicación, peso y función orgánica antes de calcular o administrar.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"guidelineRecommendations\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Contenido basado en ficha regulatoria primaria; protocolo local y microbiología pueden restringir uso.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"safetyFlags\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"CANDIDATO NO HOMOLOGADO. Revisión médica obligatoria antes de integración.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"alerts\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsiones por acumulación y lesión orgánica rara. Uso bloqueado em neonatos sem idade/bilirrubina/cálcio IV; demais doses bloqueadas sem foco, peso, alergia e função renal/hepática.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"references\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"1. Fonte regulatória primária consultada em 2026-09-18: https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?labeltype=human&query=ceftriaxone\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"2. Fonte regulatória primária consultada em 2026-09-18: https://www.cdc.gov/std/treatment-guidelines/gonorrhea-adults.htm\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"ref\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?labeltype=human&query=ceftriaxone\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"pt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"es\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ceftriaxona\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"keywords\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"dataVersion\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"clinical-data-v1-b2437901deb78b1e\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"clinicalContentSha256\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"b2437901deb78b1eeb3119ee415221916ce300d3c825122141897d5b793b513d\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"medcases-calculadora\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"schema\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"legacy-v1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sourceModule\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"infectologia.js\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"clinicalCollision\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"policySchema\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"clinical-collision-policy-v1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"policyStatus\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"proposed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"policySha256\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"54ab771c13833ef15626eed228be0a46db6443a43d52bb68d4f1dbe1468f8eaf\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"canonicalOwner\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"infectologia.js\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"decisionBasis\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"structural_score_and_git_recency_agree\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exportPolicy\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"canonical_base_with_context_variants\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"automaticFieldMerge\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\"discardSecondaryRecord\\\\\\\":false},\\\\\\\"clinicalContextVariants\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"context\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"secondary_clinical_variant\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sourceModule\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"antimicrobianos.js\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"record\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"atb\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"icon\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"💊\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"color\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"colorTxt\\\\\\\":null,\\