etyFlags y auditNotes añadidos.\\\\\\\"}},\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"pt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"es\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Ceftriaxona\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"keywords\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"rocefin\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona eurofarma\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona abl\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"rocephin\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona richet\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona generica\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"cefalosporina de 3ª geracao\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"dataVersion\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"clinical-data-v1-e61729424f211913\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"clinicalContentSha256\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"e61729424f2119133df2859fd54b61485ca0d422f660b50949e686e5f2e0905e\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"medcases-calculadora\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"schema\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"premium-v1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sourceModule\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"antimicrobianos.js\\\\\\\"}}],\\\\\\\"mc_clinical_enrichment_v1\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"schema\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"medcases.clinical-enrichment.v1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"drug_key\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"stage_a_batch\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"05\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"stage_a_reviewed_at\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-08-24\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"stage_a_source_policy\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"official_regulatory_label_admin_preparation_references\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sections\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"administracao_preparo\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"pt\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infusão IV\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Administrar por infusão intravenosa ao longo de 30 minutos; em neonatos, utilizar 60 minutos conforme a rotulagem da apresentação.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Cálcio — incompatibilidade\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Não reconstituir nem diluir com soluções contendo cálcio, como Ringer ou Hartmann. Não administrar simultaneamente com soluções IV contendo cálcio na mesma linha; em pacientes não neonatais, uso sequencial requer lavagem completa da linha com fluido compatível.\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"es\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infusión IV\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Administrar mediante infusión intravenosa durante 30 minutos; en neonatos, utilizar 60 minutos según el rotulado de la presentación.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Calcio — incompatibilidad\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"No reconstituir ni diluir con soluciones que contengan calcio, como Ringer o Hartmann. No administrar simultáneamente con soluciones IV que contengan calcio por la misma línea; en pacientes no neonatales, el uso secuencial requiere lavado completo de la línea con un fluido compatible.\\\\\\\"}]},\\\\\\\"referencias\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"pt\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DailyMed — Ceftriaxone Sodium for Injection\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Fonte oficial/regulatória consultada em 24/08/2026 para Administração/Preparo. Atualização da fonte informada: 2026-01-22.\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"es\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DailyMed — Ceftriaxone Sodium for Injection\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Fuente oficial/regulatoria consultada el 24/08/2026 para Administración/Preparación. Actualización informada de la fuente: 2026-01-22.\\\\\\\"}]}},\\\\\\\"sources\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"stage\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"A_BATCH05\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"dailymed_ceftriaxone_128bb292\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"DailyMed — Ceftriaxone Sodium for Injection\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=128bb292-d174-4769-b3e6-9f16617f31e3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"reviewed_at\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-08-24\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"updated\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-01-22\\\\\\\"}]},\\\\\\\"mc_gold_standard_v1\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PASS_CLINICAL_HOMOLOGATION\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sourceOwner\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"database/infectologia.js\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sourceField\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"ceftriaxona.mcGoldClinicalV1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"lote\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"016\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"requiredFields\\\\\\\":33,\\\\\\\"approvedSha256\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"edd955962363f9efc0d22d2a79299d1e785692bced8bf248426d86777ef530d0\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"calculationAuthorized\\\\\\\":false,\\\\\\\"publicationAuthorized\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"clinicalPackagePublicationState\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"NAO_AUTORIZADA\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ownerPublicationAuthorization\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"mission10-owner-confirmed\\\\\\\"}}\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"# Ceftriaxona\\\\n\\\\n## Clase\\\\n\\\\nCefalosporina de 3ª generación parenteral\\\\n\\\\n## Clase farmacológica\\\\n\\\\nBetalactámico inhibidor de la síntesis de pared bacteriana\\\\n\\\\n## Mecanismo\\\\n\\\\nBetalactámico inhibidor de la síntesis de pared bacteriana. El efecto debe interpretarse por indicación, formulación y exposición.\\\\n\\\\n## Farmacodinámica\\\\n\\\\nRespuesta y toxicidad dependen de exposición y población; consultar dosis y monitorización.\\\\n\\\\n## Farmacocinética\\\\n\\\\nSemivida larga; eliminación renal y biliar; alta unión proteica.\\\\n\\\\n## Indicaciones\\\\n\\\\nInfecciones sistémicas susceptibles, meningitis, gonorrea y profilaxis quirúrgica según protocolo.\\\\n\\\\n## Nombres comerciales\\\\n\\\\nNo presumir marca regional; usar solo producto correspondiente a fuentes regulatorias citadas.\\\\n\\\\n## Presentación\\\\n\\\\nViales 250/500 mg, 1 g y 2 g para IV/IM.\\\\n\\\\n## Presentaciones\\\\n\\\\nViales 250/500 mg, 1 g y 2 g para IV/IM.\\\\n\\\\n## Posología de referencia\\\\n\\\\nAdulto: 1-2 g IV/IM una vez/día o dividido; grave/meningitis hasta 4 g/día. Gonorrea: seguir guía vigente.\\\\n\\\\n## Pediatría\\\\n\\\\n50-75 mg/kg/día; meningitis 100 mg/kg/día, máximo 4 g/día. Neonatos tienen restricciones específicas. AUTOMATABLE=NO.\\\\n\\\\n## Función renal\\\\n\\\\nGeneralmente sin ajuste renal aislado; limitar/controlar si disfunción renal y hepática combinadas.\\\\n\\\\n## Función hepática\\\\n\\\\nPrecaución en enfermedad grave y disfunción renal concomitante.\\\\n\\\\n## Efectos adversos comunes\\\\n\\\\nDiarrea, náusea, erupción y reacción en sitio de administración.\\\\n\\\\n## Efectos adversos graves\\\\n\\\\nAnafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsiones por acumulación y lesión orgánica rara.\\\\n\\\\n## Efectos adversos\\\\n\\\\nDiarrea, náusea, erupción y reacción en sitio de administración. Graves: Anafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsiones por acumulación y lesión orgánica rara.\\\\n\\\\n## Contraindicaciones\\\\n\\\\nHipersensibilidad grave a cefalosporinas; evaluar reacción inmediata a otros betalactámicos.\\\\n\\\\n## Interacciones\\\\n\\\\nProbenecid puede elevar exposición; revisar anticoagulantes, nefrotóxicos, soluciones incompatibles y vacunas bacterianas vivas.\\\\n\\\\n## Monitorización\\\\n\\\\nCultivos y sensibilidad, respuesta, alergia, C. difficile, hemograma, función renal/hepática y neurotoxicidad.\\\\n\\\\n## Administración\\\\n\\\\nIV/IM; nunca mezclar o coadministrar con calcio IV en neonatos.\\\\n\\\\n## Preparación\\\\n\\\\nReconstituir según vía; lidocaína solo IM y nunca IV.\\\\n\\\\n## Infusión\\\\n\\\\nIV en unos 30 min; usar línea separada/lavada para soluciones con calcio fuera del período neonatal.\\\\n\\\\n## Embarazo\\\\n\\\\nUsar cuando esté indicado tras evaluar beneficio-riesgo.\\\\n\\\\n## Lactancia\\\\n\\\\nPaso generalmente bajo; vigilar diarrea, candidiasis o sensibilización en lactante.\\\\n\\\\n## Poblaciones especiales\\\\n\\\\nVer pediatría, función renal/hepática, embarazo, lactancia y ancianos; individualizar fragilidad y polifarmacia.\\\\n\\\\n## Orientación\\\\n\\\\nExplicar indicación, administración, adherencia y signos de alarma; no cambiar dosis sin indicación.\\\\n\\\\n## Observaciones clínicas\\\\n\\\\nConfirmar producto, concentración, vía, indicación, peso y función orgánica antes de calcular o administrar.\\\\n\\\\n## Guías\\\\n\\\\nContenido basado en ficha regulatoria primaria; protocolo local y microbiología pueden restringir uso.\\\\n\\\\n## Seguridad\\\\n\\\\nCANDIDATO NO HOMOLOGADO. Revisión médica obligatoria antes de integración.\\\\n\\\\n## Alertas\\\\n\\\\nAnafilaxia, SCAR, C. difficile, citopenias, convulsiones por acumulación y lesión orgánica rara. Uso bloqueado em neonatos sem idade/bilirrubina/cálcio IV; demais doses bloqueadas sem foco, peso, alergia e função renal/hepática.\\\\n\\\\n## Referencias\\\\n\\\\n1. Fonte regulatória primária consultada em 2026-09-18: https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?labeltype=human&query=ceftriaxone\\\\n\\\\n2. Fonte regulatória primária consultada em 2026-09-18: https://www.cdc.gov/std/treatment-guidelines/gonorrhea-adults.htm\\\\n\\\\n## Referencia\\\\n\\\\nhttps://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/search.cfm?labeltype=human&query=ceftriaxone\\\",\\\"calculationAuthorized\\\":false,\\\"clinicalApprovalGranted\\\":false}\",\"payloadSha256\":\"ed6f225c4e74236b5fabeff253ed8f5dbb02871f242a20edb5869d50b28463ee\",\"modelCalls\":0}}")
    as Map<String, dynamic>;
